{
  "kind": "rerecord",
  "why": "Chats over tmux and herdr now take two helper features the recorded hellos predate, so these recordings still replay but exercise the old path; recorded again so the corpus covers the new one. (1) `screens.host`: a Mac client naming it no longer publishes the screens of tmux and herdr terminals; the helper reads them from the multiplexer itself (attach from such a client no longer marks the terminal client-rendered; a publish from another client, the phone, still wins until it leaves), with settle-paced captures (100 ms quiet, at most every 500 ms during continuous output; a `changed: false` read captures at once; the prompt watcher samples host-read screens every 33 ms only while a native prompt is open). (2) `terminals.follow`: the Mac holds the output of a hidden tmux/herdr chat terminal after a 2 s grace (the helper stops queuing terminal.output for that observer) and follows again when the terminal is shown or the Mac reads its screen, the helper sending a fresh screen through its restore path. With them the app's cadences changed: latency is probed only while a host popover is on screen, background statistics every 15 s while a window shows and 60 s hidden or in Low Power, the sidebar branch every 10 s shown, 60 s hidden and at once after a finished command; and the chat queue now drains when a native input or question finishes. Every recorded case of the chat-over-multiplexer classes (TmuxChat, Herdr, ChatModelPicker, ClaudeTransport, SSHChat, SSHClaude, SSHPi, CodexMainThread, CodexQueue, PiChat, ChatQueue, SSHHerdr) is listed; HerdrChatIntegrationTests has no recording; left out: the pre-existing live failure ChatQueueTests/testDraggingQueueHandleReordersWithoutPasteboard (its recording stays) and the Linux classes (SSHLinuxClaude/SSHLinuxPi: no Linux test host paired when recorded).",
